  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "386054fefdbcd38d24a4b001e7c166b375ec5b7b",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/386054fefdbcd38d24a4b001e7c166b375ec5b7b",
      "message": "Accept canonical zero-group observations during owned-process census\n\nTreat a readable literal PGID zero as a known nonmember while retaining positive owned-record and leader identity checks. Add causal controls for valid zero-group entries and malformed zero forms.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:52:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "fbcd59b4e782f26612847e02ef27c97ac12dbefc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/fbcd59b4e782f26612847e02ef27c97ac12dbefc",
      "message": "Keep initialization reserve assertions within the existing file limit\n\nExpress the same output and mint assertions directly and shorten their comments; retain the 739-line limit and every funding constraint. Refs #643.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:47:57Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "70ec1753a95d1b303d342eda06f2e39e6a45b644",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/70ec1753a95d1b303d342eda06f2e39e6a45b644",
      "message": "Check correction-lock reserves without minting ADA (#643)\n\nUpdate the existing atomic initialization assertion for the new lock reserve while retaining all other output funding checks. Explicitly reject lovelace in the mint set, which caused the observed MULTIPLE_POLICIES regression during validation.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:45:07Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "bbfb4fea83d98d13662fd9c3076064bbfdf6f558",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/bbfb4fea83d98d13662fd9c3076064bbfdf6f558",
      "message": "Merge canonical watcher verification policy into permissionless recovery",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:38:23Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "b804564c0a8b691583ad09dba2f9e1c159bc4af2",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/b804564c0a8b691583ad09dba2f9e1c159bc4af2",
      "message": "Reserve correction-lock ADA for permissionless fraud recovery\n\nFund fresh correction locks for their largest typed locked datum using live ledger parameters. Preserve exact lock value, authenticated prover rewards and permissionless caller signatures. Build the canonical regression from confirmed genesis and real transition commitments. Both active and retired descendant removals pass with durable SQLite reservation recovery. Refs #643.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:36:43Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "6b9a83b0a0fb62fafacbcdfccf230becd180c714",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6b9a83b0a0fb62fafacbcdfccf230becd180c714",
      "message": "Merge pull request #764 from Anastasia-Labs/codex/lean-merge-verification\n\nSelect current merge scope and bind reusable validator evidence",
      "authorName": "colll78",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:34:39Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "248d44e2e951d8ccfcd286a15b1b2138edb1307f",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/248d44e2e951d8ccfcd286a15b1b2138edb1307f",
      "message": "Read CI merge parents from shallow commit objects\n\nThe real Actions identity artifact exposed empty revision-walker parent output in its depth-one checkout. Read ordered parents from the raw commit header so exact integration evidence remains verifiable without relaxing freshness checks. The causal shallow-checkout control and final tooling assertions are recorded in PR #764.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:25:47Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c016cfb29fc04b8e09552e38ef888aeb2d79e1c0",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c016cfb29fc04b8e09552e38ef888aeb2d79e1c0",
      "message": "Select current merge scope and bind reusable validator evidence\n\nJudge the intended target merge tree rather than a feature upstream or stale ancestor. Keep shared execution helpers at full scope while selecting tooling checks for preflight-only changes. Admit only two file validators with exact checkout, discovered inputs, Node profile, audited commands and completed CI coverage; retain distinct protocol and live acceptance gates. Verification details are recorded in the follow-on pull request.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T05:17:00Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ad587ebd06886f9ace66ee0a587c47cb1477d286",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ad587ebd06886f9ace66ee0a587c47cb1477d286",
      "message": "Refresh verification catalogue for canonical test dependencies (#643)\n\nThe declared Node and Watcher fixture dependencies expand the generated workspace dependency closure. Regenerate the required-check catalogue from the current registry. Repository-tooling tests passed 199/199, exit 0, on 2026-10-04.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T04:52:26Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "ebc9a4a3786e6436d664b210a3636c350bfec55f",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ebc9a4a3786e6436d664b210a3636c350bfec55f",
      "message": "Preserve generated lockfile formatting (#643)\n\nKeep only the declared Node and Watcher test dependency links. Parsed YAML comparison confirms all keys, values, array order and dependencies match the formatted checkpoint; repository formatting checks cover TS and Markdown, not this generated lockfile.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T04:45:04Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "9e32472c70432f44a4c281f5b2d66c7ef8dc2f7f",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/9e32472c70432f44a4c281f5b2d66c7ef8dc2f7f",
      "message": "Exercise permissionless slash custody across SQLite restart (#643)\n\nPublish the canonical fixture deployment through the current publisher and bind actual third-party slashes to authenticated prover rewards, runtime funding authority and the real reservation store. Preserve exact signed bytes, confirmations and leases across reopen. Add declared test dependencies and the existing SQL loader without relaxing strictness or timeout guards.\n\nVerification: final fault-proof and Watcher typechecks, ten-file lint, and TS/config/package/lock formatting passed on 2026-10-04. Canonical runtime and hosted acceptance remain pending. Refs #643.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T04:40:29Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "37a1f04e9c13f5020de0fb88d20f5af348a3e683",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/37a1f04e9c13f5020de0fb88d20f5af348a3e683",
      "message": "Merge pull request #762 from Anastasia-Labs/codex/deterministic-contributor-tools\n\nMake recurring contributor workflows deterministic",
      "authorName": "colll78",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T04:30:34Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "fbc69dc3016e3a025f3bb85b5ae3e86a31b58196",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/fbc69dc3016e3a025f3bb85b5ae3e86a31b58196",
      "message": "Merge pull request #760 from Anastasia-Labs/codex/683-descendant-attribution-20261003\n\nRestore per-block operator attribution when pruning descendants",
      "authorName": "colll78",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T04:11:44Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "eff85c848dedffd222864df3cc9da6c03869fb69",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/eff85c848dedffd222864df3cc9da6c03869fb69",
      "message": "Confirm owned process exit with stat-only termination observations\n\nAfter a validated SIGTERM, a leader can lose cmdline or cwd between proc\nreads. A redundant full identity observation then rejected safely completed\ngroups.\n\nBind post-signal observations to the recorded PGID and start ticks, scan\ngroup stat conservatively, and retain replacement, read-error and live-member\nrefusals before escalation or record removal. Initial full ownership\nauthorization remains strict.\n\nNormal setup under Node22 and pnpm9.15.4 produced causal RED with five passes\nand two expected failures, corrected seven passes, and fourteen passes in\nthe complete nearest file. An always-empty census mutant failed both\npreservation controls plus the live-leader control. Exact-path formatting,\nESLint and the declared Tools typecheck passed.\n\nRefs #696",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T03:59:15Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "16f5a1ea69fbbdd392b26b76b5fe0e035b9119ff",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/16f5a1ea69fbbdd392b26b76b5fe0e035b9119ff",
      "message": "Match focused test runtime to each package recipe\n\nThe guarded runner forced emulator mode on watcher tests, refusing test-only recovery constructors. Keep emulator mode for node and node-tools and use the ordinary test runtime elsewhere. A child-process case in the existing orchestration suite catches this previously untested environment regression; it failed before the fix and passed after. All eight affected watcher files pass 110 assertions from a durable worktree without weakening production storage guards.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-04T03:09:26Z"
    }
  ],
